  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed flat roofed two storey side and rear extensions by reason of their contrived and incongruous form would fail to relate appropriately to the character and appearance of the host dwelling and the terrace of which the site forms a part, as well as the visual amenities of the street scene at both Warwick Road and the rear of Denton Road. The proposals are thereby contrary to policies DMD6, DMD7, DMD8, DMD11, DMD13,  DMD14 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document, CP30 of the Core Strategy and D3 and D4 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "The proposed rear dormer by virtue of its design, scale, siting, dimensions and awkward relationship with the two-storey rear extension would give rise to a contrived and bulky form of development that would be detrimental to the visual amenities of Warwick Road and Denton Road.  Additionally, the dormer would create additional bulk to the roofscape to represent a dominant and incongruous addition and awkward relationship with the parent roofslope and the proposed first floor rear extension, thereby both unbalancing and detracting from the character and symmetry of the prevailing build form within the street scene. The proposal would therefore fail to preserve the character and appearance of the application dwelling and the wider setting, contrary to Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Core Strategy, DMD6, DMD8, DMD13 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document as well as the aims and intentions outlined within the NPPF (2021).",
    "Insufficient arboricultural evidence has been provided, in the form of BS 5837:2012 to demonstrate that there would be no impact to the nearby tree on third party land as a result of the proposed development. This tree is prominent and offers valuable amenity within the street scene and the irrevocable damage caused by the development is unjustifiable and would not be acceptable. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the advice contained within the NPPF (2021), policy G7 of the London Plan (2021) and policy DMD80 of the Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development fails to demonstrate appropriate and adequate safe pedestrian access, cycle parking and refuse and recycle storage commensurate with the more intensive residential use proposed, leading to conditions prejudicial to the free flow and safety of highway users, contrary to Policies T5 and T7 of the London Plan, CP25 and CP24 of the Core Strategy and DMD7, DMD8 and DMD47 of the Development Management Document."
  ],
